      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2015-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Inside the parentheses, \\[ \\begin{aligned} &2^0-1+5^2+0 \\\\ &\\quad = 1-1+25+0 = 25. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThen \\[(25)^{-1}\\times 5 = \\dfrac{5}{25} = \\dfrac{1}{5}.\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Evaluate inside the parentheses first, using \\(2^0=1\\)",
        "A \\(-1\\) exponent means take the reciprocal before multiplying by \\(5\\)"
      ],
